# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env (gitignored).
# The board (via CEO) provisions all paid accounts — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.
#
# This file is INSTANCE-WIDE only. Per-company setup (boardroom API key,
# LiveKit credentials per company) is done in the plugin UI at
# Company → Settings → Papervoice. See docs/MULTI_COMPANY.md for the flow.

# Paperclip control plane — instance URL. The plugin owns per-company auth.
PAPERCLIP_API_URL=

# ElevenLabs — TTS (and Scribe STT). https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Voice for the M1/direct-call fallback. Premade "Rachel" streams on every tier.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=21m00Tcm4TlvDq8ikWAM

# LLM for the agent persona
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: instance-wide LiveKit fallback. Used when a company has no LiveKit
# row filled in the Setup panel — see docs/MULTI_COMPANY.md "LiveKit project
# isolation". For separate-tenant multi-company, leave these blank and configure
# per company in the UI so each company has its own LiveKit project.
#LIVEKIT_URL=
#LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
#LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=

# ─── Per-company env-var fallback ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only if you cannot use the settings-page flow (air-gapped worker, plugin
# route unreachable). Prefer the UI: docs/MULTI_COMPANY.md leads with it and
# adding a company that way needs no restart.
#
# All four sources are merged into one companyId -> pcp_* map at startup;
# later sources win on collisions. See docs/MULTI_COMPANY.md "Air-gapped
# deployments (env-only)" for the mint procedure and gotchas.
#
#   * PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID + PAPERCLIP_BOARDROOM_API_KEY — default-company
#     binding for single-tenant deployments and for calls whose room metadata
#     omits companyId
#   * PAPERCLIP_BOARDROOM_API_KEY_<UUID_WITH_UNDERSCORES>=pcp_...
#     e.g. for companyId 8126b511-8dd2-4fa0-8a4f-22d630b83108 the var is
#     PAPERCLIP_BOARDROOM_API_KEY_8126B511_8DD2_4FA0_8A4F_22D630B83108
#   * PAPERCLIP_BOARDROOM_API_KEYS=pcp_a,pcp_b,pcp_c
#     comma-separated list; the worker asks Paperclip which company each key
#     belongs to on startup
#   * PAPERCLIP_BOARDROOM_KEYS_JSON=/etc/papervoice/boardroom-keys.json
#     JSON file shaped { "<companyId>": "pcp_...", ... } — highest priority,
#     rotates a single company's key without touching env
#
# Optional: issue id to post the post-call summary comment to. Leave unset to
# skip posting a summary (the standup still runs and can still file issues
# live).
#PAPERCLIP_STANDUP_SUMMARY_ISSUE_ID=
